 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Zero Direction:** The direction vector must not be zero-length before normalization. If the input direction is zero, normalization fails [G].
-*   **Precision:** Using `double` for coordinates and parameters is recommended to avoid precision issues during intersection tests, as seen in standard implementations [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Range Clipping:** Intersections with $t < \text{RAY\_MIN\_T}$ are typically treated as inside the volume or invalid to avoid self-intersection artifacts near the origin [S3, unofficial].
+*   **Zero Direction:** If the input direction is $(0,0,0)$, normalization fails. Implementations should guard against this or treat it as a degenerate ray [G].
+*   **Precision:** Using unnormalized directions with $t$ as distance leads to incorrect sampling positions. Always normalize or use $t$ as a scalar multiplier of the raw vector [S2, S3, unofficial].
+*   **Range Clipping:** In traversal, $t$ must be clamped to $[range\_min, range\_max]$ to prevent sampling outside the volume or at the camera plane [S3, unofficial].
 
